WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.000
Welcome to the Python basics course.

00:00:05.000 --> 00:00:15.000
Today we will learn about variables and data types.

00:00:15.000 --> 00:00:30.000
A variable is a named location in memory that stores a value.

00:00:30.000 --> 00:00:45.000
In Python, we create variables simply by assigning a value.

00:00:45.000 --> 00:01:00.000
For example: x = 5 creates an integer variable.

00:01:00.000 --> 00:01:15.000
And name = "Alice" creates a string variable.

00:01:15.000 --> 00:01:30.000
Python automatically determines the data type.

00:01:30.000 --> 00:01:45.000
This is called dynamic typing.
